.TH OPENWITTY-VOLUMED 1 "November 2026" "openwitty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openwitty-volumed \- keep the desktop volume in step with the LEWITT CONNECT 2 speaker knob
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openwitty-volumed
.RB [ \-\-mirror " | " \-\-vendor\-fallback " [" \-\-max\-increase\-db " n] | " \-\-dry\-run " | " \-\-check ]
.RB [ \-\-poll\-ms " 250..5000]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Linux kernel cannot read back the CONNECT 2's speaker volume, so turning the speaker volume
knob does not move the desktop (KDE/PipeWire) volume.
.B openwitty-volumed
reads the device (read-only) and updates the desktop's ALSA volume control to the level the
device already has: re-read first, rounded down, never unmuting. The Mute button and desktop
volume changes reach each other through the kernel without this program.
.PP
Normally it runs as the systemd user service \fBopenwitty-volumed.service\fR, switched on in
OpenWitty under Settings \(-> Desktop integration. Without a mode flag it follows the settings file:
idle while desktop sync is off, mirror mode when it is on. While the OpenWitty window is open it
hands the device to the window and takes it back afterwards. Unofficial; not affiliated with
LEWITT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mirror
Mirror mode regardless of the settings file (device read-only).
.TP
.B \-\-vendor\-fallback
Experimental and not validated on hardware: additionally apply a desktop change that the device
did not follow (after a 1.5 s grace period) through the vendor protocol \- speaker volume and
mute only, one SET, read back, never retried, at most \fB\-\-max\-increase\-db\fR (default 10)
louder per step. Requires \fBLEWITT_ALLOW_HARDWARE_WRITE=1\fR and
\fBLEWITT_ALLOW_WRITE_SPEAKER_VOLUME=1\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report decisions only; write nothing anywhere.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Diagnose the audio setup (sound card, hardware volume, kernel quirk) and exit. No OpenWitty
vendor USB access; opening the ALSA mixer can make the kernel read the device.
.TP
.BI \-\-poll\-ms " ms"
Device poll interval (default 1000).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/openwitty/openwitty.conf
Settings shared with
.BR openwitty (1)
(keys \fBdesktop_volume_sync\fR, \fBvendor_fallback\fR, \fBoutput_control\fR; all off by default).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
openwitty-volumed \-\-check
systemctl \-\-user status openwitty-volumed.service
journalctl \-\-user \-u openwitty-volumed
systemctl \-\-user disable \-\-now openwitty-volumed.service
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openwitty (1),
.BR openwitty-cli (1),
/usr/share/doc/openwitty/VOLUME_INTEGRATION.md
